* Double Kiosk System

** Description

*** Software Components:
- *Operating System*: Raspbian Pi OS 64-bit (Trixie)
- *Video System*: X11 with Multi-Pointer X (MPX)
- *Virtual X Servers*: Xephyr
- *Video Mode*: 1920x1080 (full screen)
- *Input Management*: Independent touchscreen cursors per display

*** Functionality
Upon powering on, the kiosk connects to the designated URL, which is displayed on both monitors at full screen. Users can navigate the kiosk site via touchscreen with independent control.

The kiosk supports dual users simultaneously with TRUE INDEPENDENCE:
- Each user has their own dedicated cursor
- Touch on left screen controls only left display
- Touch on right screen controls only right display
- No focus stealing or interference between users
- Fully independent browsing sessions

** Setup Instructions
1. Write the =double_kiosk_2025_10_13.img= image file to an SD card.
2. Connect both monitors using HDMI and USB cables.
3. Power on the device.

** Configuration
Configuration file: =/boot/firmware/kiosk_config.sh=

The configuration file allows users to modify the following settings:
- *URL*: Kiosk site URL
- *TOUCHSCREEN_PATTERN*: Device detection pattern (auto-detects by default)
- *ORIENTATION*: Monitor orientation (normal/right/left/inverted)
- *ENABLE_MOUSE_EMULATION*: Enable/disable mouse devices (false = better performance)
- *TOUCHSCREEN_LOG_LEVEL*: Logging verbosity (0-3)

Note: On-screen keyboard has been removed for full-screen browsing

See =SETUP_INSTRUCTIONS.md= for detailed configuration options.
** Setup on the fresh Raspbian Pi OS
***  Write an image on SD card Device - Raspberry Pi 5, Raspbian Pi OS 64-bit (Trixie)
****  Connect Ethernet cable
***  First start settings.
***  Use English Language. Use US keyboard.
****  Add user: pi - <Password>
****  WiFi: Skip
****  Default Browser: Chromium
****  Update Software
*** Install packages. sudo apt install xserver-xephyr onboard python3-xdg git
***  Raspi-config
****  /6 Advanced Options/A7 Wayland/W1 X11
****  /1 System Options/S5 Boot/B1 Console Text console 
****  /1 System Options/S6 Auto Login/To console - Yes
***  git clone git@github.com:ekazanov/double_kiosk.git
*** Copy files:
- double_kiosk/rootfs/home/pi/.profile -> /home/pi/.profile
- double_kiosk/rootfs/home/pi/010_run_xephyr.sh -> /home/pi/010_run_xephyr.sh
- double_kiosk/rootfs/home/pi/010_xephyr.sh -> /home/pi/010_xephyr.sh
- double_kiosk/rootfs/home/pi/lib/*.sh -> /home/pi/lib/ (create directory first)
- double_kiosk/rootfs/etc/xdg/openbox/rc.xml -> /etc/xdg/openbox/rc.xml
- double_kiosk/bootfs/kiosk_config.sh -> /boot/firmware/kiosk_config.sh
*** Create log directory:
- sudo mkdir -p /var/log/kiosk
- sudo chown pi:pi /var/log/kiosk
*** Reboot

** Documentation
See =SETUP_INSTRUCTIONS.md= for detailed setup, configuration, and troubleshooting information.
